<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan wheat, blend imports rise, flour falls.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan wheat, blend imports rise, flour falls.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's wheat and wheat-rye blend imports rose 21.7 percent to 89,600 tonnes in January over the December level, with nearly all the total from Kazakhstan, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee, which reports its figures to Interfax news agency, said that Russian wheat flour exports in January fell 18.1 percent month-on-month to 6,800 tonnes.</p>
<p>Wheat flour imports were down 28.3 percent to 24,400 tonnes from 34,000 tonnes in December 1996, while barley imports slipped 11 percent month-on-month to 32,600 tonnes from 36,600 tonnes. --Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
